# Root-level ignore rules. The app lives in Black-Eclipse-site/ and has its own
# detailed .gitignore; these cover the git repository root only.

# SQLite database files (WAL mode) anywhere in the tree. The previous patterns
# were the literal strings `0`, `0-shm`, `0-wal` (a truncated `*.db`), which
# matched any path segment named `0` and could silently ignore a real file.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Local dev server logs (`.dev-run2.log`, …) — never committed.
/.dev-run*.log
# Root-level launcher/test logs (desktop-refresh*.log, vitest-full.log, …).
/*.log

# Local, regenerable artifacts kept at the repository root.
# A stray root `node_modules/` can appear if a tool (e.g. vitest) runs from the
# repo root instead of Black-Eclipse-site/; it is build cache, never committed.
node_modules/
/_backups/
/reset-backups/
/opencode/

# Root-level runtime state written by a launcher started at the repository root
# (`.black-eclipse/channels/secret.key` is a generated channel-encryption key).
# Never commit it; the app's own directory has its own `/.black-eclipse/` rule.
/.black-eclipse/

# HyperFrames generated project state and capture cache. It embeds absolute
# machine paths, so it is runtime data and is never committed.
**/.hyperframes/

# Internal security assessment output. Contains reproduction detail and must not
# be published with the public repository until every finding is fixed or
# explicitly accepted.
/security/audit/
